      "losses": 0,
      "verified_on": "2026-08-12",
      "last_seen": "2026-08-12",
      "source": "run moe_stage2-ch16h, 2026-08-12, 16h budget, four dead-end directions",
      "title": "Measure achieved occupancy from the ISA before spending a round on it",
      "lever": "Before opening an occupancy or host-latency direction on a JIT-dispatched grouped GEMM, read the achieved occupancy off the shipped binary; here it was already at the register-bound ceiling (3 wg/CU), so the whole axis was a true negative.",
      "apply": "Pull the .kd note out of the AMDGPU ELF inside the loaded JIT .so (llvm-readelf --notes) and read VGPR/AGPR counts, spill, LDS bytes and block size, then divide the arch register file by the rounded VGPR count.",
      "verify": "Interleave host-side A/B probes in the same process so drift cannot manufacture a delta, and compare the resulting geomean against the frozen baseline rather than against a fresh re-time.",
      "pitfall": "Profiler VGPR counter disagreed with the descriptor (76 vs 148) -> sampled counter, not the allocation -> take the register count from the .kd descriptor.\npitfall: the compiler's min-occupancy attribute read as a cap -> it is a floor the hardware can exceed -> compare it with the achieved value before believing a low number.",
      "caution": "Also verify what the harness clock covers: when it brackets only the GPU region, host dispatch and graph-replay work sit off the measured critical path even where they would help end to end."
    },
